[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141343290","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109080#issuecomment-3141343290","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109080","id":3141343290,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67PRg6","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-31T21:08:11Z","updated_at":"2025-07-31T21:08:49Z","body":"> Take a look at #105529, where as part of the unification/clean up logic, I'm adding support for the native code to control the egl render loop.\r\n> \r\n> You should be able to rebase this PR on top of it.\r\n\r\nThanks! With that refactor, it does make the code here a lot cleaner. I've rebased this PR on that one, and added the changes that I think should be necessary, however, it doesn't actually work.\r\n\r\nThe challenge is that with PR #105529, it seems to start by creating a (0, 0) surface, and then a little bit later creating the \"real\" surface with the real dimensions. This causes problems because Godot's render thread will have already taken ownership of the EGL resources after the first surface was created, so the Java render thread can't use them to make the second surface.\r\n\r\nSo, I'll need to figure out a way to prevent creating the first surface, I guess? Although, it seems like it'd still be possible for the surface to change or be resized, which would lead to the exact same problem again...","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141343290/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3146109924","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109080#issuecomment-3146109924","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109080","id":3146109924,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67hdPk","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-02T01:50:50Z","updated_at":"2025-08-02T01:50:50Z","body":"> The challenge is that with PR #105529, it seems to start by creating a (0, 0) surface, and then a little bit later creating the \"real\" surface with the real dimensions.\r\n\r\nThe logic in the PR starts by creating a off screen pixel buffer surface first in to allow the native logic to start executing as soon as possible. Then when the Android surface is available, we switch from the off screen pixel buffer surface to the Android surface. \r\nFor prototyping I can add a flag to disable that new behavior.\r\n\r\n> because Godot's render thread will have already taken ownership of the EGL resources after the first surface was created, so the Java render thread can't use them to make the second surface.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what you mean; only the egl surface should be destroyed and recreated when the transition happens, and as you mention the same behavior should trigger when the surface is resized.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3146109924/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3152170301","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109080#issuecomment-3152170301","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109080","id":3152170301,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc674k09","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-04T20:01:49Z","updated_at":"2025-08-04T20:02:22Z","body":"> > because Godot's render thread will have already taken ownership of the EGL resources after the first surface was created, so the Java render thread can't use them to make the second surface.\r\n> \r\n> I'm not sure what you mean; only the egl surface should be destroyed and recreated when the transition happens\r\n\r\nI mean that when it creates the 2nd surface, `eglMakeCurrent()` returns `EGL_BAD_ACCESS`. I _think_ this is because the EGL context still belongs to the Godot render thread, so the Java thread can't use it. I need to do some more investigation, though.\r\n\r\n> and as you mention the same behavior should trigger when the surface is resized.\r\n\r\nYeah, the whole concept of re-creating the EGL surface is tricky together with Godot's multithreaded rendering. It seems like we'll need to synchronize both threads somehow in this case","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3152170301/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3152350195","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109080#issuecomment-3152350195","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109080","id":3152350195,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc675Qvz","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-04T20:40:54Z","updated_at":"2025-08-04T20:45:10Z","body":"> I mean that when it creates the 2nd surface, `eglMakeCurrent()` returns `EGL_BAD_ACCESS`. I _think_ this is because the EGL context still belongs to the Godot render thread, so the Java thread can't use it. I need to do some more investigation, though.\r\n\r\nHeh, actually, just ignoring the `eglMakeCurrent()` error seems to allow multi-threaded rendering to start! That call fails on the Java side, but then when the Godot render thread does it later, it succeeds, and since that's where the rendering actually takes place, things do seem to work.\r\n\r\nI need to figure out how to do this in a non-hacky way, though :-)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3152350195/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3152482865","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109080#issuecomment-3152482865","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109080","id":